      "description": "Watch Mainz 05 vs Eintracht Frankfurt highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 12, 2026. High-Octane Action in the Bundesliga The pitch was set for a riveting clash on September 12, 2026, as Mainz 05 and Eintracht Frankfurt faced off in a match defined by shifting momentum and tactical battles. In an encounter that demanded resilience from both sides, every challenge was contested with the intensity synonymous with top-flight football, keeping the 33,305 spectators on the edge of their seats until the very end. First Half Fireworks The game opened at a blistering pace, with Can Uzun breaking the deadlock in the 10th minute following an assist from Jonathan Burkardt , shortly after a strike rattled the goalpost. Mainz 05 refused to be cowed and, despite the pressure, found an equalizer in first-half stoppage time as Jonathan Burkardt volleyed home a precise finish from a Jeremiaha Maluze delivery. The drama reached a fever pitch just before the interval when Mainz missed a golden opportunity to take the lead, as Noah Atubolu saved a penalty following a foul by Raphael Onyedika on Phillip Tietz . Late Drama at the Death The second half saw tactical shifts and a renewed offensive push. Can Uzun struck again in the 60th minute, restoring the lead for Eintracht Frankfurt with a composed right-footed effort. As the clock ticked down, fresh legs from the bench, including Mario Goetze and Otto Ruoppi , looked to influence the outcome. Just when it appeared the visitors might hold on for the result, the game saw its ultimate twist in the 90th minute: Phillip Tietz emerged as the hero, firing a sensational volley into the net from an Otto Ruoppi assist to settle the affair in breathtaking fashion."
